preConditionHook:
// THE HIGH AND TIGHT FLAG (G01-14): every one of the last pullbackBars bars has
// a SMALL RANGE -- under smallBarAtrFraction ATRs -- and holds within
// nearAtrFraction ATRs of the recent highest high, so the whole "pullback" is
// one or two tiny bars pinned under the extreme. The short is the mirror below
// the recent lowest low.
//
// NOT SmallBarNearRecentExtreme, which reads a small bar near the recent LOW
// with an UP close -- buying at support. Exchanging the side is a SEPARATE RULE
// under merge decision 12 (the negate toggle gives "not A", never the mirror
// side), and this is additionally an ALL-OF-N run rather than a single bar. NOT
// ShallowPullbackFractionOfImpulse, which measures depth against the impulse leg
// instead of against bar size; the two are kept apart deliberately.
//
// THE LEVEL IS THE SHIFTED WINDOW EXTREME (merge decision 7), the highest high
// of the swingLookback bars ending one bar ago, and BOTH distances are in ATRs
// so the rule passes the shift test. ONE level and ONE ATR for the whole run of
// bars, read at the current bar -- LargeBarCountInWindow's arrangement, which is
// what keeps the stateful WFSafe_ accumulator out of the loop.
//
// RECORDED: the shifted window still OVERLAPS the flag when pullbackBars > 1
// (bar 1 is both a flag bar and inside the window). The merged pseudocode says
// the window ends one bar ago and that is what is written; the flag bars are
// small and sit under the extreme by construction, so they rarely define it.
//
// ATR is MultiWalk's WFSafe_AvgTrueRange, a ROLLING accumulator and a DIFFERENT
// FUNCTION from the plain built-in: seeded with a full N-term sum on the study's
// first calculated bar and again whenever the length changes, thereafter
// advanced as TWO SEPARATE STATEMENTS -- EasyLanguage evaluates
// S[1] + in - out left to right, and folding it to S += in - out rounds
// differently and lands on the other side of a threshold (@OJ 2015-02-20).
// AtrProfitTarget is the reference implementation with the measurements. The
// accumulator stays in the hook, which the generator emits unconditionally:
// EasyLanguage does not short-circuit and/or, so a stateful call inside a
// condition would advance every bar in EL and only on some bars in C++.
//
// The window scan mirrors EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest()/Lowest()
// call: seeded at the window's first bar (offset 1, the window being shifted by
// one), scanning the rest with a STRICT comparison so a tie keeps the earliest
// bar. Extremes is EL SOURCE, so its comparisons carry the relational tolerance
// and use el_lt / el_gt.
//
// The loop runs WITHOUT a break and clears a flag rather than abandoning the
// scan -- EasyLanguage has no loop break.
//
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope, so the hooks
// survive a double placement; every one is fully assigned each bar before it is
// read.
if (atrLenState != (int)atrLookback) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLookback; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLenState = (int)atrLookback;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLookback;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atrValue = atrSum / (int)atrLookback;
hiWin = high[1];
loWin = low[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)swingLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], hiWin)) hiWin = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], loWin)) loWin = low[i];
}
flagHi = true;
flagLo = true;
for (int kk = 0; kk <= (int)pullbackBars - 1; ++kk) {
    if (el_ge(high[kk] - low[kk], smallBarAtrFraction * atrValue)) { flagHi = false; flagLo = false; }
    if (el_ge(hiWin - low[kk], nearAtrFraction * atrValue)) flagHi = false;
    if (el_ge(high[kk] - loWin, nearAtrFraction * atrValue)) flagLo = false;
}
